This is an independently implemented DSH plugin. No source code or runtime
dependency from sixtysevenlf/dsh-blender-plugin is included.

Included components:
- worker/*.py and skills/studio-space-review/scripts/mesh_contacts.py:
  GPL-3.0-or-later, license text in legal/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt.
- Three.js 0.180.0 (MIT), bundled into lib/client.js. License: legal/three-LICENSE.
- clipper2-ts 2.0.1-18 (BSL-1.0), bundled into lib/geometry-kernel.js.
  Original license and pinned source metadata: legal/geometry-kernel/.
- esbuild is used only to build the Client and geometry kernel; it is not a customer runtime
  dependency. Its MIT license remains in the development installation.
- DSH and Cordis are host-provided peer modules. The design preset copies and
  adapts the official PTC preset (DeepSeek, MIT); source commit and digest:
  legal/dsh-ptc-baseline.json. License: legal/dsh-MIT-LICENSE. No other Host
  implementation is copied into this package.

Chinese spatial-design references adapt general principles from Anthropic
frontend-design and Paul Bakaus's Impeccable (Apache-2.0). Sources, pinned
commits, original notices, licenses and modification details are retained
under legal/aesthetic-library/. No upstream executable, automation or
telemetry is included.

Spatial concept, interior-style and composition references selectively adapt
wuciyouci/interior-design-skill (MIT), Gu Jun / arch-skills.com (documentation
CC BY 4.0), and Abhinav Bhardwaj's Skills-Architects (MIT). Modeling references
adapt sixtyseven67's dsh-skill-blender-modeling (MIT), with upstream attribution
to RobLe3 and blender-skills contributors. Pinned sources, original licenses,
notices and modification details: legal/spatial-design-library/.
The concept skill and its concept-and-moodboard reference retain CC BY 4.0;
other independently authored plugin code retains its stated license.
No source text, executable, scene or image from zwl0520/codex-blender-skill is
redistributed. The plugin's studio-realism instructions are independently
written for its existing CAD, mesh review and render workflow.

The public repository contains no furniture meshes, previews or textures.
The setup script prepares these locally from Kenney Furniture Kit and
ambientCG WoodFloor051 and Concrete034 (all CC0-1.0). Selected files are
verified against the manifest and retained unmodified. Credits and source
hashes: legal/asset-sources.json. Base colors and exhibition primitives are
generated by this plugin.

The setup script also prepares a local development runtime from:
- Blender 4.5.15 LTS, official macOS arm64 build 5afeabba6097. Blender is
  GPL-3.0-or-later with separately licensed dependencies. Copyright and
  complete notices remain under Blender.app/Contents/Resources/text/ and
  its Python installation.
- ezdxf 1.4.5 (MIT), pyparsing 3.2.5 (MIT), fonttools 4.60.1 (MIT), and
  typing_extensions 4.15.0 (PSF license). Original notices remain in
  runtime/vendor/*.dist-info. Pinned wheels: legal/python-wheels.json.

The locally assembled bundle is for development. It is not a customer
release and is not prepared for redistribution with Blender binaries;
corresponding-source, signing and platform acceptance remain separate
release work. No ODA converter or commercial DWG SDK is included.
